        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sts. VI., VII.—See Nîtis'ataka Miscellaneous Stanzas 4 and 6.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. VIII.—प्रियतमा &c. alludes to the idea that S'iva and Pâr-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "vatî form a single body, one half of which is male and the other",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "half female. न यस्मात्परः = to whom there is no superior. The two",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "lines mean that S'iva though he is so far under the dominion",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "of Love as to have his wife as one half of himself, is also the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "first as to withstanding love. The fourth line should not have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "two negatives. It means “the rest are able only to enjoy not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "to abandon.” As it stands, it may mean, “The rest can neither",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "enjoy (i. e. properly) nor abandon” &c.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. IX.—This Stanza occurs at p. 139 of the Mṛichchhakaṭi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ka with variations. सुशील in our text must be corrected to कुलशील",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "in accordance with the reading there. The other differences",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "may fairly be regarded as real variæ lectiones. श्मशानघटिका = pots",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "used in the cemetry, unholy.—Vasantatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. X.—A similar Stanza but the reverse in its tendency may",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "be seen in the Kâvyasangraha p. 28 also see p. 360.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r8",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XI.—मायाप्रयोगप्रिये might as it stands be made to yield some",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "sense by being taken with हृदये; but I think it ought to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "मायाप्रयोगः प्रिये; and after गणो there is a word omitted which I think",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "is गुणो in other places where the Stanza is found. सदैव कथितम् cor-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "responds to श्लाघ्यते. कार्कश्य and the other corresponding words",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "here have double senses. I do not see the double sense of अलीक.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "Williams gives it to mean “small” but I do not know any autho-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "rity for this, and even he does not give it as a noun in this",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "sense. स्थूलता is (1) fullness or plumpness, and (2) unwieldi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "ness or sluggishness.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r9",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XII.—गोष्ठी = conversation. It also means assembly but",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the former is preferable here.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
